---
kind: scene
id: arrival
title: The Gate
on: nightFalls
once: run
---

## The car

::bg{location="gate" time="night"}
::music{action="start" mood="dread" volume="low"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Tobias's car is parked across the ambulance bay, driver's door open, the dome light long dead.
@narrator{code="0020"}: On the dash, under the parking permit he stole in 2019, a note in his square capitals.
<match on="user.deaths">
  <when is="0">
    @nell{code="0010" mono}: Eleven o'clock. He went in at nine. He said two hours.
  </when>
  <when is="1..2">
    @nell{code="0020" mono}: I have stood here before. I know I have. The gravel remembers my shoes.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @nell{code="0030" mono emotion="numb"}: Again. The same car, the same door, the same note. The ward keeps the night on a loop and me inside it.
  </otherwise>
</match>

## The door

@narrator{code="0030"}: The gate of St. Agathe's has been chained since 1979. Someone has cut the chain. Someone has also put a new keypad on the gatepost, and it is lit.
@nell{code="0040"}: Toby? Tobias!
@narrator{code="0040"}: The ward swallows the name. Somewhere inside, very far off, a wheel squeaks once.
<branch id="goIn" prompt="The lobby doors stand open.">
  <choice id="call" label="Call him again">
    @nell{code="0050"}: Tobias Arden, you come out here right now!
    @narrator{code="0050"}: The squeak again. Closer, and then not.
    ::lure{room="lobby"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="quiet" label="Go in quietly">
    @nell{code="0060" mono}: Quiet. Whatever squeaks, it doesn't need to know my name.
  </choice>
</branch>
@narrator{code="0060"}: You step over the threshold. Behind you the gate's keypad blinks, patient as a pulse.
